+ * thread never prints its line after kernel_thread_start - so the SYSRESET
+ * write is not a hardware wall, and it is the boot thread's own context that
+ * cannot survive the release. 0110 therefore moves the whole post-release
+ * observation into the worker (poll FW_INIT_RESULT, read sentinel, reset, cm3
+ * config), leaves no GMU access after start on the boot thread, and brackets
+ * kernel_thread_start and the pause after it with markers so log54 says which
